I am lucky to have my second NAO monk running and doing well. I started
bare handed and advanced until Master, then got Frostbrand which meanwhile
is at +7 and Basic; an awful weapon indeed! With not enough AC I collected
gold for some protection, but without body armor still not enough to face
Master Kaen, I thought; so I wished for GDSM to get 10+ points more AC.[*]
Now I am feeling quite un-monkish, wielding a weapon and getting all that
messages about cumbersome armor. Anyway; usually Frostbrand is so effective
that it seems to make no sense to return to bare-handed combat and become
a Grand Master, and besides the boring messages the body armor seems also
no problem with the usual crtitters. But it turned out that I had problems
to hit Master Kaen at all! With help of a wand of sleep and the drain life
spell he's dead now, but I wonder if there will be any problems with such
a weapon/armor combination with other high level monsters later.

Janis

[*] BTW, my monk has not yet found any single scroll of enchant armor.


